Liquidity 

&#xa0;

Our need for capital has typically resulted from the acquisition of containers and chassis, trucks, tractors and trailers required to support our growth and the replacement of older equipment as well as periodic business acquisitions. We are frequently able to accelerate or postpone a portion of equipment replacements or other capital expenditures depending on market and overall economic conditions. During the first nine months of 2020, we postponed a portion of our equipment purchases in order to increase our available cash in light of the economic disruption and uncertainty resulting from COVID-19. We will continue to monitor economic conditions and contemplate adjustments to planned capital expenditures as needed throughout the ongoing COVID-19 pandemic. Expenditures are being evaluated based on those that must happen, those that can be deferred to a later period, and those that are capable of being canceled. We have, during the past recent years, obtained capital through cash generated from operations, revolving lines of credit and long-term debt issuances. We have also periodically utilized operating leases to acquire revenue equipment.

&#xa0;

